<header><p class="st-kicker">other · Balkans and Hungary</p><h1 class="st-title">Independent State of Croatia</h1><p class="st-meta">1941 CE – 1945 CE · capital Zagreb</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Axis puppet state ruled by Ante Pavelić's Ustaše, notorious for genocide against Serbs, Jews and Roma during the Second World War.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>As German forces invaded the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/kingdom-of-yugoslavia">Kingdom of Yugoslavia</a>, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ustase">Ustaše</a> leader <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/slavko-kvaternik">Slavko Kvaternik</a> proclaimed the Independent State of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/croatia">Croatia</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zagreb">Zagreb</a> on 10 April 1941, ending the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/banovina-of-croatia">Banovina of Croatia</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ante-pavelic">Ante Pavelić</a> returned from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a> as Poglavnik. The state included Croatia and all of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bosnia">Bosnia</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/herzegovina">Herzegovina</a>, but in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/treaties-of-rome-1941">Rome Agreements</a> of May 1941 ceded much of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dalmatia">Dalmatia</a> to Italy.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ustase">Ustaše</a> regime was a one-party dictatorship under German and Italian protection, with a nominal king, the Italian <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/prince-aimone-duke-of-aosta">Prince Aimone</a>, as Tomislav II from 1941 to 1943. It pursued the murder, expulsion and forced conversion of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/serbs">Serbs</a> and the extermination of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jews">Jews</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/romani-people">Roma</a>, in camps such as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jasenovac-concentration-camp">Jasenovac</a>. Much of its territory was contested by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yugoslav-partisans">Partisans</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chetniks">Chetniks</a>.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>As Partisan forces advanced, the state collapsed in May 1945. Its troops and civilians fleeing to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/austria">Austria</a> were turned back at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bleiburg-repatriations">Bleiburg</a> and many were killed by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yugoslav-partisans">Partisans</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ante-pavelic">Pavelić</a> escaped to <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/argentine-republic">Argentina</a>. The territory became part of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/socialist-federal-republic-of-yugoslavia">Socialist Federal Republic of Yugoslavia</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/independent-state-of-croatia.jpg" alt="Independent State of Croatia" width="320" height="213"><figcaption>Image: public domain by User:Zscout370 · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Croatia_(1941%E2%80%931945).svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1941 CE – 1945 CE</dd><dt>Century</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>other</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>bureaucratic</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Zagreb</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Ante Pavelić, Slavko Kvaternik</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Catholic Christianity, Sunni Islam</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Croatian</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/croatia">Croatia</a>, <a href="/countries/bosnia-and-herzegovina">Bosnia and Herzegovina</a>, <a href="/countries/serbia">Serbia</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>NDH, Nezavisna Država Hrvatska</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1943&amp;focus=independent-state-of-croatia" aria-label="Independent State of Croatia on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5058 563 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Independent State of Croatia lay"><image href="/maps/w